**a. ΔG° for the reaction DMEA + CH₃COOH → DMEAH⁺ + CH₃COO⁻**

The equilibrium constant for this acid–base reaction is  

\[
K_{\text{eq}}=\frac{K_a(\text{CH}_3\text{COOH})}{K_a(\text{DMEAH}^+)}
            =\frac{1.8\times10^{-5}}{6.0\times10^{-10}}
            =3.0\times10^{4}
\]

\[
\Delta G^\circ =-RT\ln K_{\text{eq}}
               =-(8.314\;\text{J mol}^{-1}\text{K}^{-1})(298\;\text{K})\ln(3.0\times10^{4})
\]

\[
\ln(3.0\times10^{4})=10.3089\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\Delta G^\circ =- (8.314)(298)(10.3089)= -2.55\times10^{4}\;\text{J mol}^{-1}
\]

\[
\boxed{\Delta G^\circ = -2.55\times10^{4}\ \text{J mol}^{-1}\;(\text{or }-25.5\ \text{kJ mol}^{-1})}
\]

---

**b. ΔH° from the calorimetric data**

* Initial temperature (intercept of the linear region)  

\[
T_i = y(x=0)=19.03^{\circ}\text{C}
\]

* Final temperature (plateau)  

\[
T_f =31.84^{\circ}\text{C}
\]

\[
\Delta T = T_f-T_i = 12.81^{\circ}\text{C}
\]

Mass of the solution at the end‑point  

\[
m_{\text{sol}}=m_{\text{water}}+m_{\text{acid}}+m_{\text{DMEA}}
               =107.17\;\text{g}+7.84\;\text{g}+12.00\;\text{g}=127.01\;\text{g}
\]

Heat capacity (treated as water)  

\[
C_{\text{sol}} = (4.184\;\text{J g}^{-1}\!^{\circ}\text{C}^{-1})(127.01\;\text{g})
               = 5.31\times10^{2}\;\text{J °C}^{-1}
\]

Heat released  

\[
q_{\text{rxn}} = C_{\text{sol}}\Delta T
                = (5.31\times10^{2}\;\text{J °C}^{-1})(12.81^{\circ}\text{C})
                = 6.81\times10^{3}\;\text{J}
\]

Moles of DMEA added at the equivalence point  

\[
n_{\text{DMEA}}=\frac{12.00\;\text{g}}{89.14\;\text{g mol}^{-1}}
                =0.1346\;\text{mol}
\]

\[
\Delta H^\circ = -\frac{q_{\text{rxn}}}{n_{\text{DMEA}}}
               = -\frac{6.81\times10^{3}\;\text{J}}{0.1346\;\text{mol}}
               = -5.06\times10^{4}\;\text{J mol}^{-1}
\]

\[
\boxed{\Delta H^\circ = -5.06\times10^{4}\ \text{J mol}^{-1}\;(\text{or }-50.6\ \text{kJ mol}^{-1})}
\]

---

**c. ΔS° from ΔG° = ΔH° – TΔS°**

\[
\Delta S^\circ = \frac{\Delta H^\circ-\Delta G^\circ}{T}
               =\frac{(-5.06\times10^{4})-(-2.55\times10^{4})}{298\;\text{K}}
               =\frac{-2.51\times10^{4}}{298}
               =-8.4\times10^{1}\ \text{J mol}^{-1}\text{K}^{-1}
\]

\[
\boxed{\Delta S^\circ = -84\ \text{J mol}^{-1}\text{K}^{-1}}
\]

(The sign is negative, as found in the calculation.)

